-- title:
--   Germ of j(q^q)-j^q vanishing along the first component
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ whose non-units contain the image of $q$, and a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak P$ of level $N_0q$ over $R_q$ (the data `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`), the residue field of $A$ being algebraically closed of characteristic $q$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$, together with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ of $O$ onto the valuation subring obtained by pulling $A$ back along the inclusion of the fixed field of the inertia subgroup of $A$ in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, a ring map $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ whose composite with $e_O$ and these inclusions is the structure map $R_q \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$, and a ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ given by reducing the image of $e_O$. Assume the scheme `DRLevel.fibre0` attached to $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$, namely the pullback of the Igusa map $X_0$-side `toBase0 N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$, is integral, and that $\mathfrak X_O$, the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$, is integral. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `… 1` supplied by the package, and write $x_n$ for its image in $\mathfrak X_O$ under the first projection followed by the zeroth of these morphisms followed by the base-change map `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`. Let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-base-changed modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)`, subject to two normalisations: on constants, $\varphi$ sends the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $\mathfrak X_O$ determined by $a \in O$ to the image of $a$ in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ under $e_O$ and the inclusions; on the finite Igusa chart (whose preimage under the first projection is assumed nonempty), $\varphi$ sends the germ in the function field of the section coming from $a \in$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` to the Laurent series of $a$ with coefficients pushed into $\overline{\mathbf Q}$. Finally assume the specialisation $h_{sp_0}$: the image in $\mathfrak X_O$ of the generic point of `fibre0` under the zeroth package morphism followed by `bcMap` specialises to $x_n$. The conclusion is that there exists $t_F$ in the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at $x_n$ with $\varphi$ of its image in the function field equal to $j(q^q) - j(q)^q$, that is `ProlongationTuple.jQFun N₀ q - ProlongationTuple.jFun N₀ q ^ q` (the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{qExpand}\,q\,j$ minus the $q$-th power of $j$), and whose image under the specialisation map `stalkSpecializes hsp₀` from the stalk at $x_n$ to the stalk at that generic point lies in the maximal ideal.
--
--   This is the Kronecker congruence $j(q^q) \equiv j(q)^q$ read on the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over an unramified base $O$: at a crossing point of the special fibre, the function $j(q^q)-j^q$ has a germ vanishing at the generic point of the first of the two components, which is the component on which the $q$-isogeny is Frobenius. It feeds the analysis of the local coordinates at the crossings, being used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation).
